    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "narration_text": "The heart of it is the revision lifecycle. A chapter change is drafted, submitted, reviewed, and either sent back or approved. Then it's published, and it can be rolled back. Two rules stood out. Authors can't approve their own work. And review state and deploy state are separate fields, so nobody confuses approved with live.",
